WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.375
This slide sets the default for Intune
targeting, so it's worth getting right.

2
00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:07.925
By default each policy goes
to a dynamic device group.

3
00:00:07.925 --> 00:00:11.198
Microsoft's current
guidance, checked October 29,

4
00:00:11.198 --> 00:00:14.951
is to prefer assignment filters
where they meet the need,

5
00:00:14.951 --> 00:00:20.300
because dynamic device groups add processing
delay, and Book 05 now says the same.

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:24.688
Send user settings to user groups
and device settings to device groups.

7
00:00:24.688 --> 00:00:27.967
The exception is tier and
role: filters can't read

8
00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:31.901
device extension attributes,
so those stay in group rules.

9
00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:36.600
And underneath it all, a device rule
can never read its owner's attributes.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.240
Next, how device attributes get written.
